#!/usr/bin/env bash

lord --verbose << "EOF"
Run a command like 'grep -r '\\Table[{]' -C100 0*'

(or equivalently, just look at the output of that command in ./TABLES)

and then try to refactor the definition of \Table{...} in master.tex
so that:

1. Most of the repeated boilerplate that shows up every time you USE that command
   is included instead in the definition itself.

2. But whenever any of the tables NEED to be different, the \Table{...} definition
   should allow adding those differences as needed, either by passing in values for
   certain optional parameters, or by wrapping the \Table{...} invocation in some
   other stuff to change its behavior.

3. Try to reproduce the current behavior of all the existing \Table{...} invocations,
   if it is possible to do so without adding excessive cruft to the \Table{...} definition.
   The goal is to simplify the invocations of \Table{...} throughout the codebase,
   so if there's a BIT of semantic change, it's worth it if we can get a significant
   simplification of the implementation.
EOF
